WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Gatut: (We seek) refuge in God from the rejected devil.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Bism Allah Arrahman Arraheem

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
In the name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.000
We are in Sura 67, Kingship (Al-Mulk).

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:21.000
[67:1] Most exalted is the One in whose hands is all kingship, and He is Omnipotent.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Well, I have to stop here.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.000
The verse says very clearly that in God is all the Kingship.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:41.000
So, Kingship means that He is the sole and the only authority in this whole universe.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.000
And He is also Omnipotent according to this verse.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:53.000
We also learn from the Quran that God grants Kingship to whomever He wills, and He grants it to the believers.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:03.000
In other words, we know that people who worship God alone and follow God's commandment alone,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:09.000
God promised them that they will be sovereign, or. kings or queens on earth.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:14.000
In other words, they have everything that they need.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Everything that they need will be in their fingertips without, you know, the headache of a celebrity

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:30.000
that we know, you know, needs bodyguards, protection from FBI, or you cannot go to Burger King

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.000
to eat if you want because that's the headache of being a celebrity.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:41.000
You have a prison on your own, but God's servants, the believers, have all this and can still

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:46.000
enjoy this, and they have anything that they want. And I think that's the biggest, you know,

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:53.000
even the richest person in the world cannot do that because they will go everywhere and everybody

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:59.000
or some people or some news reporter will follow them. You know, Sam Donaldson will follow them

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.000
and ask questions and all that.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.000
So, the believers don't have that kind of headache.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.000
The same goes with the, you know, financial problems.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:16.000
They don't need 10 million dollars, but they have everything that they need.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:24.000
They get good transportation. They get anything that they need, good clothings, without being, you know,

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.000
without worrying that the IRS will get into their pocket or something.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.000
Gatut: So,... Dr. Khalifa: All the food they can eat.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.000
Gatut: All the food that they can eat. That's right. Which is what we have today. Alhamdu Lillah.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:42.000
So, God grants kingship to whomever He wills, and according to the Quran, that is the believers.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.000
Verse 2, The Purpose of Our Life.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:55.000
[67:2] The One who created death and life for the purpose of distinguishing those among you who would do better.* He is the Almighty, the Forgiving.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:06.000
God created death and life to distinguish the human beings who are the real believers

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.000
and who are the wishy-washy ones.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:18.000
We all know that the purpose behind creating us here in this life and the whole universe is

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:25.000
because billions of years ago, we doubted God's Supreme Authority.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:29.000
In other words, there is one guy who said "well, I can be a god besides God."

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:35.000
And we, all the human beings, this is before the creation of the heavens and the earth and,

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:41.000
you know, our stay here, we don't show our firm stand for God.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:47.000
In other words, we said "well, this guy who was Satan, he may have a point."

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.000
In other words, "let's give him a try. Let's test him."

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:55.000
So, we didn't have a firm stand as opposed to the angels, for instance, who said that

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.000
"there is no way that anybody except God can rule the universe."

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:06.000
So, God gave us the second chance to redeem ourselves and this is because of His Mercifulness.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:10.000
God doesn't need to prove anything.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.000
He already knew.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.000
He knows what's gonna happen.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:19.000
There's no future for Him because as far as He is concerned, everything is past. Everything has taken place.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.000
Only He knew it.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:27.000
But we need to affirm to ourselves, in other words, on the Day of Judgment,

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:35.000
everybody will see with their own eyes that this is what they do, that they do not really believe or they are a real believer.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.000
So, it is the human beings who need the affirmations.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:42.000
So, there'll be no excuses on the Day of Judgment.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.000
And verse says that "He is Almighty, the Forgiving."

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:55.000
He is Forgiving because even though we committed the blasphemy, we committed the crime

00:04:55.000 --> 00:05:03.000
that makes us, you know, here in this life right now, He didn't send us outright to Hell, but He gave us a second chance.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:12.000
The angels said, of course, at the time when we were created "why don't You just send them all to Hell?"

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:15.000
God says "I know what you do not know."

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.000
Because God knows that some of the human beings will be redeemed.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.000
And these are the believers.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.000
Number 3,

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:35.000
[67:3] He created seven universes in layers. You do not see any imperfection in the creation by the Most Gracious. Keep looking; do you see any flaw?

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:40.000
[67:4] Look again and again; your eyes will come back stumped and conquered.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:53.000
[67:5] We adorned the lowest universe with lamps, and guarded its borders with projectiles against the devils; we prepared for them a retribution in Hell.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:06:01.000
[67:6] For those who disbelieved in their Lord, the retribution of Gehenna. What a miserable destiny.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:07.000
[67:7] When they get thrown therein, they hear its furor as it fumes.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.000
Number 8,

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:17.000
[67:8] It almost explodes from rage. Whenever a group is thrown therein, its guards would ask them, "Did you not receive a warner?"

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:26.000
[67:9] They would answer, "Yes indeed; a warner did come to us, but we disbelieved and said, 'GOD did not reveal anything. You are totally astray.'"

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:33.000
[67:10] They also say, "If we heard or understood, we would not be among the dwellers of Hell!"

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:38.000
[67:11] Thus, they confessed their sins. Woe to the dwellers of Hell.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:49.000
Verse number 3, we learn from here that our universe is not the only universe that God created.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:58.000
The scientists, the astronomers, are still trying to determine, you know, the limit or the borders of the universe where we live in.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:07.000
And according to God, and this will be proven, IN SHAA ALLAH, in the near future, that

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:11.000
this universe is only one of the seven universes that God created.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:26.000
Dr. Khalifa: (unintelligible)

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.000
Gatut: Our universe...

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:29.000
Dr. Khalifa: (unintelligible)

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.000
Dr. Khalifa: Go ahead.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:45.000
Gatut: Our universe we live in, we live in the, a little dot called the planet Earth, which is located in the solar system.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.000
We have our own star, which is the sun.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:56.000
And our star is one of the hundreds of thousands of stars in our galaxy, which is the Milky Way galaxy.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:04.000
And our Milky Way galaxy is one of the billions of galaxies in the universe that, you know, they stopped counting

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:07.000
because they couldn't get the total number.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:17.000
But the universe that we live in, which according to rough calculation is probably about 26

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:20.000
billion light years across, is only the smallest universe.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:26.000
That means that it takes 26 billion years for light to travel.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:32.000
Billions with a B. So, that's how awesome is the innermost universe.

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:37.000
And there are six other universes around the innermost universe.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:42.000
And everything is, all the seven universes, according to the Quran, is in God's hand.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:09:02.000
However, the innermost universe is also, according to verse number five, is actually the prison cell for Satan.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:06.000
Because he cannot go beyond our universe.

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:15.000
In Sura 72, verse 9, and also in Sura 15, verse 18, there's the same reference of, you know,

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:25.000
the guard of the universe that, you know, the jinns and Satan cannot go beyond because they will be pursued by projectiles.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:37.000
But nobody can find any flaw in God's creation.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:46.000
You know, we just look and lay down at a dark night when the moon is, you know, very young and look at the stars.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:48.000
I used to do camping a long time ago when I was young.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:52.000
And I always, you know, lie down and look at the dark night and look at the stars.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:10:00.000
And I'm always, you know, never ceased to be amazed how all these can become into being.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:10.000
Our sun is just one of the dim stars in the universe, in our universe which is the Milky Way galaxy and

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.000
billions of galaxies like that.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:21.000
And yet, we cannot imagine how vast is the universe because until now there is no way

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:25.000
that we can even go to our closest neighboring star.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.000
And not to mention the neighboring galaxy.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.000
Verse 4 says this perfectly,

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:35.000
[67:4] Look again and again; your eyes will come back stumped and conquered.

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:39.000
And that's, at least that's my impression when I look at the stars.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:48.000
We also learn from verse 5 that the lowest universe, which is our universe, is adorned with lamps, which is stars.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.000
This is... We know that lamp is the source of light.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:56.000
And we know that our sun is one of the stars.

00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:02.000
So, what is implied here is probably that only our universe has stars.

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:07.000
So, we don't know how the outer universes, the second, the third universes look like.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:27.000
We also learn from this Sura in verse 7, 8 and 9, how terrible is the condition in Hell.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:35.000
We know that Hell is reserved only for those people who go out of their way to reject

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.000
or deny God's Greatness.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:49.000
And therefore, when people go there, people go there on their own volition because

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:53.000
despite of all these warnings that God sent through the messengers, through the scriptures,

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:59.000
and through all the signs that God manifested to the people, they still insist on going

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:04.000
there. And therefore, it's like they already deserve what they get over there.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:08.000
But God explains here how terrible is the condition in hell.

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:13.000
It is like, Hell has its own personality.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:19.000
I mean, Hell has its own, Hell can be so angry towards the disbelievers because when the disbelievers were sent there

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:22.000
group by group, Hell can even, you know, sort of talk back to them.

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:25.000
"Suffer. What do you do? Why did you...?"

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:27.000
"Can I have more?"

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:31.000
In some other verses in the Quran Hell says "can I have more of these people?"

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:32.000
You know, because...

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:35.000
It's like, you know, a very, very savage beast.

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:38.000
But Hell is simply the absence of God.

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:44.000
In other words, these people cannot stand to become close to God because they did not develop

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:46.000
their soul enough in this life.

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:49.000
And therefore on the Day of Judgment, they have to run away from God.

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:53.000
They couldn't stand the presence of God. And

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.000
that absence of God is really actually Hell.

00:12:55.000 --> 00:13:03.000
Because in some of the verses in the Quran, we learn that Hell is also described by darkness, by hopelessness,

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:07.000
also fire where people are roasted there and never die.

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:12.000
So, there is no excuse for the disbelievers when they go there because they have been warned here

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:17.000
as, with, you know, as best allegory as human language can find.

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:32.000
As a matter of fact, in verse 9, we know that disbelievers will, what is the word, they will accept the blame. This...

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:39.000
[67:9] ...."Yes indeed; we had a warner, but we disbelieved and said, 'GOD did not reveal anything. You are totally astray.'"

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:46.000
And this is exactly what majority of the people will say when one quotes, you know, from the scripture, you know,

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:52.000
one is conveying the word of God, they say "we don't believe you. You are far off. You are strange."

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:56.000
So, that's what they say in this life and in the Hereafter, they will admit that.

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:04.000
And they also said in verse 10 "if we heard or understood, we would not be among the dwellers of Hell."

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:07.000
Thus in verse 11, they actually confess their sins.

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:19.000
I think, if there's any questions or comments or anything, give it at the forum.

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:38.000
Gatut: Any comments or...?

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:40.000
Dr. Khalifa: Any questions?

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:47.000
Wait. As usual, I have a comment on (unintelligible) in the heaven or the sky.

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:55.000
We have here this list of Prayers, schedule for Prayers, an eternal schedule.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:57.000
It is correct forever.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:05.000
You can see in the whole year, the sunrise and sunset, by the minute.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:08.000
You could have extended it to the second and it would be exactly accurate.

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:15.000
You look here at January 1st, the sunrise at a certain time, the sun will rise exactly at that time.

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:20.000
The sunset at that time, it will exactly be at that time. So, there is no flaw in God's system.

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:25.000
We know exactly when Halley's Comet is gonna come back.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:28.000
It comes every 76 years.

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:33.000
And sure enough, right on time, there it is coming, at that point in time.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:40.000
Even though Halley's Comet in an aberration. It looks like an aberration, though it's not. It is not

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.000
So, this is why God says in 4,

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:46.000
[67:4] Look again and again; your eyes will come back stumped and conquered.

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:48.000
You are looking for a flaw.

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:50.000
You will not find one.

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:59.000
And we have a shared demonstration as to how the moon, we see only one side of the moon,

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:04.000
even though it is rotating around itself and around the earth, but this movement is synchronized

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:10.000
so precisely that if it is off by a fraction of a second, we would see the other side of the moon.

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:19.000
We look at poetry describing the moon that is thousands of years old, and they have been looking at the same side of the moon.

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:25.000
So, I just wanted to emphasize that because we have a demonstration right here.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:28.000
The flawless nature of God's creation.

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:34.000
So, these words of the Quran are flawless as well.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:40.000
Back to Gatut.

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:44.000
Gatut: Verse 12.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:51.000
[67:12] As for those who reverence their Lord, when alone in their privacy, they have attained forgiveness and a great recompense.

00:16:55.000 --> 00:17:02.000
Before we go to that page, I'll just comment here that it's very important that the belief has to be

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:10.000
also subjected to the test of whether we are believing because of the crowd or whether we are believing because of our own conviction.

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:17.000
And majority of the people, if they say they believe, that is because usually this is the norm in the society.

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:22.000
In other words, if the norm in the society is that the people believe in God,

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:30.000
if they don't believe in God, they say openly "I don't believe in God", then they're kind of like sore fingers sticking out.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:36.000
So, they don't want to be in that position. They go along with the crowd even though, in their heart, they don't really believe.

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:44.000
And this is why the words "when alone in their privacy" is very important in my opinion because

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:50.000
even when the believer is by himself or by herself, he still observes God.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:55.000
I mean, there's no difference whether he or she is in the group or by himself or herself.

00:17:56.000 --> 00:18:01.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, fasting is a good example of that because fasting is a strictly private (unintelligible). Gatut: Exactly.

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:09.000
You only... You have to be a believer in God, because you can drink or eat anywhere,

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:13.000
where nobody can see you, no human beings can see you, only God sees you.

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:15.000
So, this is a good example.

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:23.000
Gatut: That reminds me of a story from some sister who said, when the husband is not there, you say "well,

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:26.000
you can eat, you can drink, the husband is not here", you know.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:34.000
But, you know, people who said that, seriously, they did not realize how deep, it's not just simply

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:40.000
something out of skin, it is something that the believer has the conviction in their heart. So,

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:48.000
it's not because of the husband or the wife or the parents or, you know, in-laws that we fast or that we observe God, that's because of our convictions.

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:55.000
Dr. Khalifa: And when a need arises here in this community, the charity fund in the drawer.

00:18:55.000 --> 00:19:02.000
The people are putting money there and they put this envelope and they write the name of the person that it goes to. And it's anonymous.

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:07.000
I try very hard to read the handwriting, but there is no way.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:10.000
I have failed 100% of the time.

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:14.000
But the person who's putting money in there anonymously, who sees this person?

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:23.000
There's a good number of believers here who believe in God in privacy, because what is the credit they are getting?

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:25.000
They know they're getting the credit from God.

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:35.000
And we know that God writes in other verses in the Quran that if you give to charity publicly, it is good, but if you give it secretly, it's even better and remits more of your sins.

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:41.000
And obviously the people who are doing this, they know that this is the truth, they know that God will give them the credit.

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:51.000
There is no reason in the world for them to put money there, anonymously, except for knowing that God will give them... they get the credit from God.

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:56.000
So, this is a perfect example of this verse here, 12.

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:58.000
Mã Shã Allãh.

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:10.000
Gatut: [67:13] Whether you keep your utterances secret, or declare them, He is fully aware of the innermost thoughts.

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:19.000
[67:14] Should He not know what He created? He is the Sublime, Most Cognizant.

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:24.000
This is sort of a rhetorical question.

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:33.000
God who created the heavens and the earth and everything in them. Of course, He knows what, you know, what,

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:39.000
everything that He created. He's fully aware of all the creation that He made.

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:50.000
I mean, in the Quran, there is even a verse that says "not a single leaf falls without Him being knowing all that." So,

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:55.000
if we know, if we can count, if it is possible to count how many trees are there in the world

00:20:55.000 --> 00:21:01.000
and if it is possible to count how many leaves in every tree, which is impossible for any human being,

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:04.000
but God knows every single leaf that falls.

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:10.000
That is how far, we cannot imagine how great is God.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:13.000
So, we cannot even hide anything from God.

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:18.000
You know, the children are usually very very, still very innocent.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:23.000
And they used to be, you know, talk to them about, you know, God and...

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:30.000
The best way would be, in my experience, they can lie to you, but we told them that you cannot lie to God.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:34.000
You can lie to your parents, you can lie, but God will always know.

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:38.000
So, in the end, they are the ones who keep saying this all the time.

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:43.000
God always knows whether we declare anything or we keep it secret.

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:47.000
15.

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:54.000
