[67:19] Have they not seen the birds above them lined up in columns and spreading their wings? The Most Gracious is the One who holds them in the air. He is Seer of all things.

00:27:57.000 --> 00:28:00.000
Here God is talking about the law of aerodynamics.

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:10.000
We learn from the Khutba today, which is actually one of the, for those who missed the Khutba today,

00:28:10.000 --> 00:28:17.000
the video program that will be shown starting tomorrow or next week, everywhere is

00:28:17.000 --> 00:28:26.000
is a very good example of how a 20th century or 21st century human being can appreciate

00:28:26.000 --> 00:28:32.000
the facts that have been expounded in a book written 1400 years ago.

00:28:33.000 --> 00:28:40.000
All this detail about everything that only 50 to 100 years ago, some human beings started to learn

00:28:40.000 --> 00:28:43.000
has been in the Quran for 1400 years.

00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:51.000
And here we know that, first of all, the birds fly because God decided

00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:54.000
them to fly using the shape of the wings and the body.

00:28:54.000 --> 00:28:59.000
And this kind of shape and principle a human being start to learn and then

00:28:59.000 --> 00:29:02.000
they copy it and they make aeroplanes, they make helicopters with the same principle.

00:29:03.000 --> 00:29:09.000
In other words, how this 100 tons 747, for instance, can take off into the air.

00:29:10.000 --> 00:29:17.000
Simply because the shape of the wing is such that when you move the object, there will be less

00:29:17.000 --> 00:29:22.000
density of the air on top of the wing than below the wing. So, the whole thing will be lifted.

00:29:22.000 --> 00:29:27.000
So, that's the same design that God has made for the birds' wing.

00:29:27.000 --> 00:29:36.000
This is the principle of aerodynamics that is not considered well known, but yet all this has been around for millions of years.

00:29:40.000 --> 00:29:44.000
[67:19] Have they not seen the birds above them lined up in columns and spreading their wings? ...

00:29:44.000 --> 00:29:50.000
We know that the formation the birds fly, again this is also a principle from aerodynamics.

00:29:50.000 --> 00:29:57.000
The birds, God teaches the birds to fly in a certain pattern because certain pattern will be the most efficient to reduce the drag.

00:29:58.000 --> 00:30:02.000
We know that the drag is the biggest challenge for anything that moves in the air.

00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:09.000
And this kind of formation is now actually being copied by, for instance, if you see Thunderbirds

00:30:09.000 --> 00:30:17.000
F-16 from the Air Force. They always fly in a certain pattern because that pattern will reduce the drag that

00:30:17.000 --> 00:30:22.000
each particular plane will experience.

00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:26.000
Most of us probably know this principle when we drive in the interstate.

00:30:26.000 --> 00:30:35.000
If you drive 70 miles per hour and there's 18 wheelers 70 miles per hour in front of us, we tend to follow them. Because

00:30:35.000 --> 00:30:43.000
we're basically having a reduced drag by following them and we can consume... we can conserve more fuel by driving that way.

00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:48.000
So, that's also a principle of aerodynamics and it's also mentioned in the Quran here.

